('127.612.d.1.E',3,'Lines that run side by side and never meet, such as in a straight bob, are called:','["parallel lines", "curved lines", "broken lines", "diagonal lines"]'::jsonb,0,'Parallel lines give structure.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.E',4,'A function of parallel lines in hair design is to create a:','["faded look", "uniform, structured look", "messy look", "wild, random look"]'::jsonb,1,'Parallel lines produce consistency.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.F',3,'Using lines that differ sharply, such as straight bangs with curly lengths, is an example of:','["transitional lines", "parallel lines", "contrasting lines", "repeated lines"]'::jsonb,2,'Contrast adds interest.','original'),
