('127.612.d.1.J',3,'Hair color choices are often based on a client''s skin tone and:','["shoe size", "birth month", "eye color", "height"]'::jsonb,2,'Coloring should harmonize with natural features.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.J',4,'A client with cool skin undertones generally looks best in hair shades that are:','["gold only", "warm only", "neon", "cool-toned"]'::jsonb,3,'Matching undertones is flattering.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.K',3,'The level system numbers hair shades from 1 (darkest) to 10 (lightest). It creates a logical structure for describing:','["color", "rent", "cuts", "payroll"]'::jsonb,0,'Levels describe lightness and darkness.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.K',4,'A level 5 hair color is lighter than a level:','["9", "3", "7", "10"]'::jsonb,1,'Higher numbers are lighter.','original'),
('127.612.d.1.L',3,'Red, yellow, and blue are the primary colors. Mixing two primaries creates a:','["neutral", "primary color", "secondary color", "tertiary color"]'::jsonb,2,'Secondary colors come from two primaries.','original'),
