('127.613.d.2.C',3,'Interest earned only on the original amount is called simple interest, while interest earned on the original amount plus past interest is called:','["compound interest", "loan interest", "penalty interest", "flat interest"]'::jsonb,0,'Compound interest grows faster.','original'),
('127.613.d.2.C',4,'How much simple interest is earned in one year on $1,000 at 5 percent?','["$5", "$50", "$100", "$500"]'::jsonb,1,'1,000 x 0.05 = 50.','original'),
('127.613.d.2.D',3,'The longer funds stay in a savings account earning interest, the more they grow. This is the time value of:','["goods", "debts", "money", "taxes"]'::jsonb,2,'Time makes savings grow.','original'),
('127.613.d.2.D',4,'Starting to save at age 20 rather than 40 generally results in a larger balance by retirement because of more time for:','["fees", "spending", "loans", "compounding"]'::jsonb,3,'Time boosts growth.','original'),
