('127.616.d.1.G',3,'A drug dependency rehabilitation center is a social service that helps people overcome:','["boredom", "fatigue", "addiction", "hunger"]'::jsonb,2,'Rehab centers treat substance dependence.','original'),
('127.616.d.1.G',4,'A crisis hotline and a counseling center are both examples of social services that support people''s:','["travel", "car repair", "shopping", "mental health"]'::jsonb,3,'Services provide help.','original'),
('127.616.d.1.H',3,'A condition in which a person has false beliefs that others are trying to harm them is called:','["paranoia", "anxiety", "confidence", "creativity"]'::jsonb,0,'Paranoia involves suspicion.','original'),
('127.616.d.1.H',4,'Which condition is characterized by hallucinations, delusions, and disorganized thinking?','["a sprain", "schizophrenia", "hunger", "a cold"]'::jsonb,1,'Schizophrenia is a serious mental disorder.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.A',3,'A health care worker notices a patient''s tone of voice and gestures and adjusts the way he speaks. This is adapting communication to the patient''s:','["jokes", "wardrobe", "needs", "wants"]'::jsonb,2,'Good communicators adjust their messages.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.A',4,'If a client is anxious, a calm voice and simple words are ways to:','["avoid the client", "ignore feelings", "raise stress", "adapt communication"]'::jsonb,3,'Adapting helps understanding.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.B',3,'Eliminating distractions, making eye contact, and summarizing what you heard are techniques that minimize communication:','["barriers", "tools", "paths", "bridges"]'::jsonb,0,'Listening skills reduce barriers.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.B',4,'A noisy room, a language difference, and a rushed manner are all communication:','["bridges", "barriers", "goals", "tools"]'::jsonb,1,'Barriers interfere with understanding.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.C',3,'A responsive worker listens and thinks before replying; a reactive worker responds:','["slowly", "with care", "without thinking", "calmly"]'::jsonb,2,'Responsive communication is thoughtful.','original'),
('127.616.d.2.C',4,'When a client shouts, a responsive reply is to stay calm and:','["walk away", "argue", "shout back", "acknowledge the feelings"]'::jsonb,3,'Calm responses de-escalate.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.A',3,'Psychiatrist, counselor, psychologist, and social worker are all career opportunities related to mental:','["health", "travel", "wealth", "fitness"]'::jsonb,0,'Many careers support mental wellness.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.A',4,'Which career helps people through talk therapy and may require a master''s degree?','["pilot", "licensed counselor", "accountant", "welder"]'::jsonb,1,'Counselors provide therapy.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.B',3,'A group that includes a doctor, a nurse, a social worker, and a therapist working together for a patient is called a:','["fan club", "crowd", "multidisciplinary team", "committee of one"]'::jsonb,2,'Teams share expertise.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.B',4,'A benefit of the multidisciplinary team is that each member brings different:','["uniforms", "schedules", "salaries", "expertise"]'::jsonb,3,'Teamwork improves care.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.C',3,'A caregiver who thinks about how a choice will affect a patient before acting is justifying the consequences of:','["decisions", "weather", "payday", "fashion"]'::jsonb,0,'Decisions have outcomes.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.C',4,'Explaining why you chose a treatment option and what might result shows that you can justify the:','["hours", "consequences", "colors", "costs only"]'::jsonb,1,'Justification includes outcomes.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.D',3,'A trained student helps two classmates settle a disagreement by listening to both sides. This is peer:','["pressure", "review", "mediation", "tutoring"]'::jsonb,2,'Mediators help resolve conflicts.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.D',4,'Negotiation in conflict resolution aims for a result that is acceptable to:','["one side", "neither side", "only the mediator", "both sides"]'::jsonb,3,'Both parties give and gain.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.E',3,'Learning and correctly using terms such as ''anxiety,'' ''diagnosis,'' and ''therapy'' is mastering mental health:','["vocabulary", "games", "maps", "recipes"]'::jsonb,0,'Accurate terms prevent confusion.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.E',4,'Writing a patient''s symptoms clearly and accurately in a record is called:','["guessing", "documentation", "gossip", "advertising"]'::jsonb,1,'Records need precise language.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.F',3,'Individual therapy, group therapy, and medication are examples of mental health treatment:','["games", "crimes", "options", "costs"]'::jsonb,2,'Several approaches exist.','original'),
('127.616.d.3.F',4,'A treatment where several people with similar concerns meet together with a therapist is called:','["family dinner", "a rally", "a lecture", "group therapy"]'::jsonb,3,'Group therapy provides shared support.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.A',3,'Keeping a patient''s information private and sharing it only with those who need it follows the principle of:','["confidentiality", "curiosity", "publicity", "gossip"]'::jsonb,0,'Privacy builds trust.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.A',4,'Sharing a client''s story on social media would violate:','["hospital rules", "ethical practice", "none", "good manners only"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics protect clients.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.B',3,'Failure to give the standard of care expected, which harms a patient, is called:','["compliance", "generosity", "negligence", "empathy"]'::jsonb,2,'Negligence is a legal issue.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.B',4,'A health care worker could be sued for malpractice if a patient is harmed because the worker:','["followed the rules", "took notes", "asked questions", "did not follow professional standards"]'::jsonb,3,'Malpractice involves failing a duty.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.C',3,'A scope of practice is the set of duties that a professional is legally allowed and trained to:','["perform", "ignore", "avoid", "hide"]'::jsonb,0,'Staying within scope protects patients.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.C',4,'A nursing assistant performing a task that only a licensed nurse is allowed to do would be going beyond the:','["work schedule", "scope of practice", "uniform policy", "parking rules"]'::jsonb,1,'Roles are defined by law.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.D',3,'Patients have the right to be informed, to refuse treatment, and to be treated with:','["limited care", "secrecy", "respect and dignity", "no information"]'::jsonb,2,'Client rights protect choice.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.D',4,'A client''s right to choose may be limited if the person is a danger to self or others. This is a circumstance that can:','["cancel privacy", "end all rights", "remove all care", "alter client rights"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety can override some choices.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.E',3,'Acting out a patient who refuses medication in class helps students understand client rights through:','["role-playing", "reading only", "guessing", "lectures only"]'::jsonb,0,'Dramatizing makes cases real.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.E',4,'In a dramatized case study, students practice responding to a client''s choices while protecting the client''s:','["uniforms", "rights", "lunch", "wages"]'::jsonb,1,'Role-play builds understanding.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.F',3,'HIPAA is a federal law that protects the privacy of patients'' health:','["hospital names", "insurance rates", "information", "doctor salaries"]'::jsonb,2,'Legislation sets standards of care.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.F',4,'Laws that require licensed professionals to report suspected abuse help set standards for:','["parking", "advertising", "uniforms", "client care"]'::jsonb,3,'Laws protect patients.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.G',3,'The Texas Department of State Health Services is a regulatory agency that sets and enforces rules for health:','["care", "travel", "sports", "fashion"]'::jsonb,0,'Agencies regulate care.','original'),
('127.616.d.4.G',4,'A regulatory agency may inspect facilities and take action against a provider that does not meet:','["hobbies", "standards", "wishes", "trends"]'::jsonb,1,'Agencies enforce rules.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.A',3,'Unexplained bruises and fearful behavior may be signs of an abusive:','["game", "holiday", "situation", "meal"]'::jsonb,2,'Workers must recognize abuse.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.A',4,'A health care worker who suspects abuse is generally required by law to:','["ignore it", "gossip", "wait a year", "report it"]'::jsonb,3,'Mandatory reporting protects victims.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.B',3,'Staff members who stay calm when a patient suddenly becomes agitated are able to anticipate and adapt to changing:','["situations", "menus", "weather", "schedules only"]'::jsonb,0,'Flexibility is a key skill.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.B',4,'A patient''s mood can change quickly, so a worker must be prepared to:','["leave", "adjust the approach", "follow a script only", "ignore it"]'::jsonb,1,'Adaptation improves care.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.C',3,'If a patient collapses, an appropriate emergency action is to call for help and begin:','["a conversation", "lunch", "first aid or CPR if trained", "paperwork"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergencies require quick action.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.C',4,'In an emergency, health care workers should follow the facility''s emergency:','["fashion", "gossip", "menus", "procedures"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans guide response.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.D',3,'Washing hands, wearing gloves, and using safe lifting techniques practice personal and client:','["safety", "marketing", "speed", "fashion"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety protects everyone.','original'),
('127.616.d.5.D',4,'Keeping walkways clear and spills cleaned up helps ensure the safety of both workers and:','["managers only", "clients", "vendors only", "visitors only"]'::jsonb,1,'Safe environments prevent injury.','original'),
('127.616.d.6.A',3,'Patient charts, lab results, and billing records are examples of health care:','["fashion", "menus", "data", "gossip"]'::jsonb,2,'Data guides care.','original'),
('127.616.d.6.A',4,'Health care data must be collected and shared in ways that protect patient:','["speed", "profit", "fashion", "privacy"]'::jsonb,3,'Dissemination follows rules.','original'),
('127.616.d.6.B',3,'Blood pressure cuffs, thermometers, and computers are examples of equipment used in delivering mental health and health:','["services", "games", "recipes", "fashions"]'::jsonb,0,'Equipment supports service delivery.','original'),
('127.616.d.6.B',4,'Grouping devices by their purpose, such as monitoring or recording, is how you:','["ignore equipment", "classify equipment", "destroy equipment", "avoid equipment"]'::jsonb,1,'Classifying organizes knowledge.','original'),
('127.616.d.6.C',3,'A student should use technology only at the level their training allows, which is employing technology consistent with their:','["address", "salary", "level of training", "schedule"]'::jsonb,2,'Training sets limits.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_79_v1'
from (values
('127.616.d.6.C',4,'A trainee who is not certified to operate a device should not use it without:','["food", "music", "speed", "supervision"]'::jsonb,3,'Use technology within training.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
